Commit 053b61e ("increment \$VERSION after 0.500 release") bumped lib/App/karr.pm to 0.501 but left bin/karr:7 and bin/karr-foundation:6 at 0.500, so t/67-bin-version.t has been failing on main ever since:

    #   Failed test 'bin/karr $VERSION (0.500) matches App::karr (0.501)'
    #   Failed test 'bin/karr-foundation $VERSION (0.500) matches App::karr (0.501)'
    t/67-bin-version.t (Wstat: 512) Tests: 6 Failed: 2

Verified red at 053b61e itself, i.e. it is not the fault of anything on top of it. That is the only failing file in a full `prove -l t/` run of 161 files / 1097 tests (found while verifying #171).

The fix is the two version lines; the more interesting question is why the post-release bump is a manual step that can bump one of three places. Whoever takes this should decide whether the bump belongs in a single place the other two read, or whether t/67 running before the commit is enough.
2026-08-15 14:49 Fixed in bea9b7a: bin/karr:7 and bin/karr-foundation:6 to 0.501, matching lib/App/karr.pm. Scope was the two numbers only, no new bump.

Checked the tooling before hand-editing, as asked. t/67-bin-version.t is the spec: each script must carry a literal 'our $VERSION = ...;' equal to $App::karr::VERSION, and the line must stay literal because the rewrite plugins only replace an existing assignment while their insert fallback needs a 'package' statement these scripts lack. History confirms hand maintenance: the numbers were last set in 2b29403 by hand, and the automated post-release bump 053b61e touched Changes + 54 lib/ files and nothing in bin/.

Left unresolved on purpose, filed as #180: by the plugin defaults the bump SHOULD have covered bin/ (:ExecFiles is a default finder of RewriteVersion/BumpVersionAfterRelease, and @Basic's ExecDir does populate it), yet it demonstrably did not. Changing dist.ini on that guess would be cargo cult, so it is a ticket, not part of this fix.

